    "finalText": "Done. The URL shortener is complete and verified:\n\n- **Stack**: Laravel 11.57 / PHP 8.3, Eloquent + migrations on the provided MySQL (`bench`), DB settings read exclusively from `DB_*` env vars (removed the scaffolded `.env` DB lines so nothing is hard-coded).\n- **Routes**: registered `routes/api.php` with `apiPrefix: ''` in `bootstrap/app.php`, so paths are exactly `/links`, `/links/{code}`, `/r/{code}` — no `/api` prefix.\n- **Controller**: manual JSON parsing + validation in `LinkController` so every error response (`409`, `404`, `422`, malformed body) carries an `error` field; auto-generated 8-char codes retry on collision, duplicate custom codes → 409, redirects use atomic `increment('clicks')` then 302 to the stored URL.\n- **start.sh**: executable, runs `php artisan migrate --force` then `php artisan serve --no-reload --host=0.0.0.0 --port=8000`; README gained a \"Starting the server\" section.\n- **Verified**: 39/39 curl-based requirement checks passed, restart persistence confirmed (clicks 3 → 4 across a full stop/start), `php artisan test` green, DB reset to a clean state and port 8000 left free."
